@startuml 10_deployment
!include ../style.iuml
title Deployment diagram: demonstration machine and target
skinparam nodeFontStyle bold

node "Reviewer's browser" as BR <<device>> {
  artifact "HTTP client\n(httpOnly cookie + CSRF token)" as CLI
}

node "Machine or server (Windows 11 or Linux)" as HOST <<device>> {

  node "Python 3.10 to 3.14 process" as PY <<execution environment>> {
    component "Reviewer API\n(uvicorn, serve_access.py --queue)" as API
    component "Rule engine" as ENG
    artifact "rules/core.yar\nrules/*.json" as RULES
  }

  node "Celery worker" as WK <<execution environment>> {
    component "Tasks: process_claim, deal,\nexpire, relay_sweep, reconcile" as TASKS
  }

  node "Container claimguard-mongo" as MG <<Docker>> {
    database "MongoDB 7\n(--auth, 127.0.0.1:27017)" as MDB
  }

  node "Container claimguard-redis" as RD <<Docker>> {
    database "Redis 7\n(no persistence, 127.0.0.1:6379)" as RDS
  }

  node "Ollama (local)" as OL <<service>> {
    artifact "gemma3:4b" as GEM
  }

  node "Offline scripts" as OFF <<execution environment>> {
    component "Audited review\n(run_audited_review, llm_adapter)" as REVIEW
  }

  folder "Files (logs)" as FS {
    artifact "audit.jsonl + anchor\nsecurity_audit.jsonl" as LOGS
  }
}

cloud "Hosted provider (Featherless)\nopen model" as HOSTED <<external service>>

CLI --> API : HTTPS (TLS is the deployment's job)
API --> MDB : pymongo
API --> LOGS : append-only writes
API ..> ENG
ENG ..> RULES
WK --> MDB
WK --> RDS : message queue
REVIEW --> GEM : explanations (local model)
REVIEW ..> HOSTED : explanations (hosted option)
WK ..> GEM : to be wired (injected model)

note bottom of WK
  Celery workers need Linux (Docker); on Windows the
  demonstration runs the tasks in "eager" mode, inside
  the API process. The queue's AI step receives an
  injected model; the production adapter is not built:
  without a model the deterministic text is kept.
end note

note right of HOSTED
  Synthetic data only. With real data you would
  need an on-premise model or a processing agreement.
end note
@enduml
